  "captionStyle": "nick-display",
  "script": "Apple is about to drop at least 5 new products this September.\nFirst: iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max. A20 Pro chip on 2 nanometers, a variable-aperture camera, a smaller Dynamic Island, and a new Dark Cherry color.\nThe catch? Rumors put them up to $300 pricier.\nSecond: the headliner \u2014 Apple's first foldable, the iPhone Ultra.\n5.5 inches closed, 7.8 unfolded \u2014 basically an iPad mini that fits in your pocket.\nTouch ID instead of Face ID, dual batteries, and a hinge built to hide the crease.\nThe price? Somewhere between $2,000 and $2,500.\nThird: Watch Series 12 \u2014 faster chip, bigger battery, same look.\nFourth: Watch Ultra 4, possibly thinner with upgraded sensors \u2014 though that's a single source, so squint.\nAnd fifth, the real wildcard: a new boss.\nJohn Ternus runs his first keynote as CEO \u2014 Tim Cook officially becomes Executive Chairman on September 1. That part isn't a rumor.\nWhat you won't see: the standard iPhone 18. That one moved to March.\nThe event lands September 8 or 9; preorders the same week.\nSo \u2014 the $2,000 foldable, or the Pro: which one's your money on?\nTell me in the comments.\n",
